{"step_index":68,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-31T01:08:28Z","thinking":"If a business number search on the main Bizno page yields no results, the site defaults to showing a recent company list. However, directly accessing an article page with an unknown business number displays a specific \"no information\" title. The title/heading on the article page will reflect company name if a business is found in the database.\n\n\nExamining the provided data, I'm identifying the columns and their corresponding meanings within the dataset, focusing on details like company name, business registration number, and status (e.g., \"폐업\"). This involves cross-referencing information across multiple rows to understand the data's structure. Comparing two rows reveals that various fields like address and legal registration numbers are inconsistently populated, requiring careful data mapping.\n\n\nIdentifying relevant industry columns within the Bizno data and the user's specific instruction to use the \"비즈인포산업명\" column for 업종 (industry) information is key. The instruction to exclude \"거\" implies filtering for accurate data only.\n\nExamining provided rows, I'm interpreting various fields such as registration number, industry category, and company details to confirm accurate data extraction and proper column mapping. The user wants accurate data, specifically industry information.\n\n\nAnalyzing how to reconcile industry classifications. The 국세청산업분류 hierarchy maps to specific user columns. Cross-referencing 국세청 분류 with 업종분류 confirms data mapping consistency.\n\nIdentifying that the \"비즈인포산업명\" column in the user's data corresponds to NICE BizINFO 업종. The \"거\" exclusion suggests filtering out imprecise data.\nI'm thinking through how to approach this.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Batch fetcher and parser script for all 500 companies","UserFacing":false},"CodeContent":"const fs = require('fs');\nconst path = require('path');\n\nconst rawFile = 'C:/Users/lg/.gemini/antigravity/brain/fc47ed12-b523-4d84-9421-40e6756ddcef/scratch/input_raw.txt';\nconst cacheDir = 'C:/Users/lg/.gemini/antigravity/brain/fc47ed12-b523-4d84-9421-40e6756ddcef/scratch/cache';\n\nif (!fs.existsSync(cacheDir)) {\n  fs.mkdirSync(cacheDir, { recursive: true });\n}\n\nconst lines = fs.readFileSync(rawFile, 'utf8').split(/\\r?\\n/).filter(l => l.trim().length > 0);\nconsole.log(`Loaded ${lines.length} lines from input`);\n\nconst rows = lines.map((line, idx) => {\n  const parts = line.split('\\t');\n  return {\n    idx,\n    originalCols: parts,\n    charge: parts[0] || '배현명',\n    status: parts[1] || '',\n    name: parts[2] || '',\n    bno: (parts[3] || '').replace(/[^0-9]/g, ''),\n    rep: parts[4] || '',\n    zip: parts[5] || '',\n    addr: parts[6] || '',\n    tel: parts[7] || '',\n    fax: parts[8] || '',\n    homepage: parts[9] || '',\n    email: parts[10] || '',\n    empCount: parts[11] || '',\n    bizItem: parts[12] || '',\n    corpNo: parts[13] || '',\n    settleMonth: parts[14] || '',\n    catMajor: parts[15] || '',\n    catMid: parts[16] || '',\n    catSub: parts[17] || ''\n  };\n});\n\nconsole.log(`Parsed ${rows.length} rows.`);\n\nasync function fetchBizno(bno) {\n  const cachePath = path.join(cacheDir, `${bno}.html`);\n  if (fs.existsSync(cachePath)) {\n    return fs.readFileSync(cachePath, 'utf8');\n  }\n\n  const url = `https://bizno.net/article/${bno}`;\n  try {\n    const res = await fetch(url, {\n      headers: {\n        'User-Agent': 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/120.0.0.0 Safari/537.36'\n      }\n    });\n    const text = await res.text();\n    fs.writeFileSync(cachePath, text, 'utf8');\n    return text;\n  } catch (e) {\n    console.error(`Fetch error for ${bno}:`, e.message);\n    return null;\n  }\n}\n\nasync function runBatch() {\n  const concurrency = 10;\n  let running = 0;\n  let done = 0;\n  const total = rows.length;\n\n  for (let i = 0; i < total; i += concurrency) {\n    const chunk = rows.slice(i, i + concurrency);\n    await Promise.all(chunk.map(async (r) => {\n      if (r.bno && r.bno.length === 10) {\n        await fetchBizno(r.bno);\n      }\n      done++;\n      if (done % 50 === 0 || done === total) {\n        console.log(`Progress: ${done}/${total} (${((done/total)*100).toFixed(1)}%)`);\n      }\n    }));\n    // small delay to be polite\n    await new Promise(res => setTimeout(res, 100));\n  }\n\n  console.log('Batch fetch complete!');\n}\n\nrunBatch();\n","Description":"Batch fetcher script for bizno.net","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\lg\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\fc47ed12-b523-4d84-9421-40e6756ddcef\\scratch\\batch_fetch.js","toolAction":"Writing batch fetch script","toolSummary":"Create batch fetch script"}}]}
